      "root_cause_candidate": "The `rtm_get_nexthop()` function in the IPv4 nexthop subsystem allocates a fixed-size netlink socket buffer using `NLMSG_GOODSIZE` instead of dynamically calculating the required message size, causing buffer overflow warnings when handling large nexthop groups.",
      "evidence_points": "The patch modifies `net/ipv4/nexthop.c` by replacing `alloc_skb(NLMSG_GOODSIZE, GFP_KERNEL)` with `nlmsg_new(nh_nlmsg_size(nh, op_flags), GFP_KERNEL)` in `rtm_get_nexthop()`, and updates `nh_nlmsg_size()` to compute the correct size based on the nexthop group configuration and operation flags."
    },
